{
  "info": {
    "name": "Corretoria",
    "description": "Coleção da API do Corretoria.\n\nExecute de cima para baixo: os scripts de teste populam {{adminToken}}, {{userId}} e {{token}} automaticamente, e nenhuma requisição precisa ser preenchida à mão.\n\nA sequência é re-executável: o cadastro gera login e e-mail únicos a partir de {{runId}}, e o usuário criado é excluído no fim.\n\nCada requisição afirma o status esperado e, nos erros, o campo `type` do ProblemDetail — é o `type`, não o status, que distingue erros que compartilham o mesmo código.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "adminToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "otherUserId", "value": "1" },
    { "key": "runId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "senhaAtual", "value": "senhaSegura123" },
    { "key": "senhaNova", "value": "novaSenha456" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Autenticação",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login admin (salva adminToken)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('devolve um token Bearer', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.type).to.eql('Bearer');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', body.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"login\": \"admin.demo\",\n  \"password\": \"admin12345\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"] },
            "description": "Administrador de demonstração, semeado pela migration V3. É a única via de obter ROLE_ADMIN, já que o autocadastro público o recusa."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login corretor",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('token emitido', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().token).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"login\": \"corretor.demo\",\n  \"password\": \"corretor12345\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login cliente",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('token emitido', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().token).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"login\": \"cliente.demo\",\n  \"password\": \"cliente12345\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login inválido (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('type authentication-failed', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().type).to.include('/problems/authentication-failed'));",
                  "pm.test('não revela se o login existe', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().detail).to.eql('Login ou senha inválidos'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"login\": \"corretor.demo\",\n  \"password\": \"senha-errada\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"] },
            "description": "A resposta é idêntica à de um login inexistente. Diferenciar os dois casos permitiria enumerar contas válidas."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Usuários",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Cadastro de corretor (201, salva userId)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Login e e-mail únicos por execução, para a coleção poder rodar mais de uma vez.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('runId', String(Date.now()).slice(-8));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('cabeçalho Location presente', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('nunca devolve a senha', () => pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('password'));",
                  "pm.test('CEP normalizado para 8 dígitos', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(body.addresses[0].zipCode).to.eql('60000000'));",
                  "pm.test('links HATEOAS presentes', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body._links.self.href).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body._links.users.href).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Corretor Postman {{runId}}\",\n  \"email\": \"corretor.{{runId}}@email.com\",\n  \"login\": \"corretor.{{runId}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{senhaAtual}}\",\n  \"roles\": [\"ROLE_REALTOR\"],\n  \"addresses\": [\n    {\n      \"street\": \"Rua das Flores\",\n      \"number\": \"100\",\n      \"complement\": \"Sala 21\",\n      \"neighborhood\": \"Centro\",\n      \"city\": \"Fortaleza\",\n      \"state\": \"CE\",\n      \"zipCode\": \"60000-000\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "users"] },
            "description": "Endpoint público. Observe que o CEP entra com máscara e é gravado com 8 dígitos — a normalização é do VO ZipCode."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Cadastro de cliente (201)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('papel ROLE_CUSTOMER concedido', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().roles[0].name).to.eql('ROLE_CUSTOMER'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Cliente Postman {{runId}}\",\n  \"email\": \"cliente.{{runId}}@email.com\",\n  \"login\": \"cliente.{{runId}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{senhaAtual}}\",\n  \"roles\": [\"ROLE_CUSTOMER\"],\n  \"addresses\": []\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "users"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login do usuário criado (salva token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"login\": \"corretor.{{runId}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{senhaAtual}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Cadastro inválido: campos faltando (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('type validation-error', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().type).to.include('/problems/validation-error'));",
                  "pm.test('agrega os erros por campo', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(Object.keys(pm.response.json().errors).length).to.be.above(1));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"email\": \"\",\n  \"login\": \"\",\n  \"password\": \"\",\n  \"roles\": []\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "users"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Cadastro inválido: e-mail duplicado só na caixa (409)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('type duplicate-resource', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().type).to.include('/problems/duplicate-resource'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Sósia\",\n  \"email\": \"CORRETOR.{{runId}}@EMAIL.COM\",\n  \"login\": \"sosia.{{runId}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{senhaAtual}}\",\n  \"roles\": [\"ROLE_REALTOR\"],\n  \"addresses\": []\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "users"] },
            "description": "O e-mail difere do já cadastrado apenas na caixa. O 409 é evidência da regra de negócio: o VO Email normaliza para minúsculas antes da checagem de unicidade. Sem isso, este cadastro passaria."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Cadastro solicitando ROLE_ADMIN: proibido (403)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('type forbidden-operation', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().type).to.include('/problems/forbidden-operation'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Escalonamento\",\n  \"email\": \"escalonamento.{{runId}}@email.com\",\n  \"login\": \"escalonamento.{{runId}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{senhaAtual}}\",\n  \"roles\": [\"ROLE_ADMIN\"],\n  \"addresses\": []\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "users"] },
            "description": "Tentativa de escalonamento de privilégio pelo endpoint público. Recusada antes de qualquer acesso ao banco."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Busca por nome via admin (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('envelope paginado com bloco page', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().page).to.have.property('totalElements'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users?name=Corretor",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "users"],
              "query": [{ "key": "name", "value": "Corretor" }]
            }
          }
        },
